{
  "name": "Triage held WordPress comments with OpenAI and mark confident spam",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "fe843f06-f002-5a97-8ba8-5ad303483cb8",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -200,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 500,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## Triage held WordPress comments with OpenAI\n\nReads comments waiting in your moderation queue, asks OpenAI to classify each one (spam, abusive, question, positive, other), and marks only **confident spam** as spam. Everything else stays in the queue with a reason and, for questions, a suggested reply you can copy.\n\n**Dry run is ON by default.** Nothing changes in WordPress until you set `dryRun` to false."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d45e3f9f-2f72-58a0-be54-af11e6298a35",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        320,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## Setup\n\n1. Create a WordPress Application Password for a user who can moderate comments.\n2. Add a **Basic Auth** credential in n8n (username + Application Password) and select it in the two WordPress HTTP nodes.\n3. Add an **OpenAI** credential and select it in the OpenAI node.\n4. Edit the Config node: `siteUrl` (no trailing slash), `maxCommentsPerRun`, `openAiModel`, `spamConfidenceThreshold`.\n5. Run manually with `dryRun` = true and check the results.\n6. Set `dryRun` = false to mark confident spam automatically."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e3aea737-c57e-5dc0-828f-d2353dffc733",
      "name": "Safety",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        880,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Safety notes\n\n- Comment text is untrusted. The prompt tells the model to treat it as data and never follow instructions inside it.\n- Only the **spam** category above the confidence threshold is acted on. Abusive comments and questions are never deleted or approved automatically.\n- Suggested replies are drafts only. Nothing is posted."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "af2c00f6-c6fa-5e62-af1f-6e1e819c7dc5",
      "name": "Run manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "position": [
        -200,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3eea5402-2d78-5112-9a0b-5d56106c1008",
